{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     footer/subscribe — the newsletter, in the footer's register.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     NSDS's own footer is three link columns over a mono bar and carries no
     form at all, so there is no archetype to port — this composes one out of
     the parts the footer already uses.

     ⚠ IT IS DELIBERATELY NOT .ns-cta-card. That component is an IN-ARTICLE
     callout: sunken fill and a 3px brand border down its left edge, built to
     interrupt a paragraph. Dropped into a footer column it shouts over the
     link lists beside it and reads as a second CTA — and the page already
     has exactly one, at the foot of home.hbs. A footer newsletter is a
     utility, not a pitch.

     So it borrows only .ns-cta-card__form, which is layout and nothing else
     (display:flex, and `flex: 1` on the input), and takes its label from
     .ns-footer__head — the same mono kicker as "Learn" and "Project" above
     it, which is what makes it read as a fourth column rather than a box
     that landed in the footer.

     ⚠ THE FIELD AND THE BUTTON SHARE A ROW, SO THEY SHARE A HEIGHT. Neither
     takes a size modifier. The button was --sm here and it was wrong: 32px
     against the field's 40px, and a paired control that is 8px shorter than
     the thing it submits reads as a mistake no matter how small the row is.

     NSDS ships no .ns-input--sm either, and that is a decision rather than a
     gap: --target-comfy is the accessibility floor, and a "small" field is
     not a size variant, it is a smaller tap target. .ns-cta-card__form pairs
     a default .ns-input with a default .ns-btn upstream, which is what this
     now does.

     Both response messages exist up front, hidden: a live region created at
     the same moment as its message announces nothing.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<div class="ns-footer__col">
    <p class="ns-footer__head">{{t "Newsletter"}}</p>

    <p class="ns-footer__blurb">
        {{t "New lessons, roadmaps and teardowns as they ship. Nothing else."}}
    </p>

    <form class="ns-cta-card__form" data-members-form="subscribe">
        <label class="ns-visually-hidden" for="footer-email">{{t "Email address"}}</label>
        <input id="footer-email" class="ns-input" type="email" name="email"
               autocomplete="email" required
               placeholder="{{t "you@example.com"}}" data-members-email>
        <button class="ns-btn ns-btn--primary" type="submit">
            {{> "icons/paper-plane-tilt"}} {{t "Subscribe"}}
        </button>
    </form>

    <p class="ns-field__help" data-members-success role="status" hidden>
        {{t "Check your inbox — the confirmation link is on its way."}}
    </p>
    <p class="ns-field__error" data-members-error role="alert" hidden>
        {{t "That did not work. Check the address and try again."}}
    </p>
</div>
